{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789817611,"nonce":"+aJDuOK64CD9uQCpeTIMyIDnxwQ=","title":"a static call binds by bare method name to another class's runtime row","message":"`F1.fromFloat(3.0)` on a user class `F1` that declares `static function fromFloat(f:Float):Int` lowers to `SIMD4i32_from_float`: the call site fails LLVM with \"Unsupported cast from F64 to Vector { element: F32, count: 4 }\". `haxe.Int64.fromFloat(3.0)` does the same. The Haxe body is compiled and in the module; the call never reaches it.\n\nReproducer:\n\n    class F1 {\n      static function fromFloat(f:Float):Int { return Std.int(f) * 2; }\n      static function main() { Sys.println(fromFloat(3.0)); }\n    }\n\nCause: four MIR call probes fall back to a runtime-mapping scan by METHOD NAME ALONE when the class-qualified lookup misses -- `find_static_method_by_name_and_params` in `stdlib_static.rs` (symbol with a qualified name whose class is not a mapped class), `call/mod.rs` STATIC_SEARCH (`find_unique_static_by_name_and_params` even when the symbol names its owner), `resolved_method.rs` STDLIB FALLBACK (Field callee on a known class), and `stdlib_runtime.rs` `find_unique_by_method` on the instance path. `rayzor.SIMD4i32.fromFloat` is the only static `fromFloat` row, so every scan picks it.\n\nFix: a symbol that carries an owner (qualified name) is looked up under that owner only; the bare-name scan is for owner-less symbols. The Field-callee path additionally consults `StaticSigIndex::indexed_declares_static` -- a class whose source declares the method is called by that body.\n\nNot fixed here: `find_unique_by_method` on the instance path (`stdlib_runtime.rs`), which no longer receives `Int64.fromFloat` once the typer emits a static call for `pkg.Type.method(..)` on an abstract, but is still a by-name scan.","files":null}]}